  "releaseNotes": "- Publishes citations only when a safe HTTP(S) original entry is supplied,\n  consistently across live streams, historical replay, SDKs and API callbacks\n- Keeps internal resource locators and documents without an original entry in\n  tool provenance rather than presenting them as clickable reference sources\n- Displays each inline citation as its source title or filename plus a stable\n  number, with bounded long titles and full names in the source list\n- Preserves ordinary Markdown labels, tool output and durable history while\n  filtering old references without changing event cursors or callback results\n- Cleans optional source metadata independently so a malformed excerpt or state\n  cannot hide an otherwise valid original link\n- Reuses Runtime `1.0.0-beta.28`; no sandbox template rebuild is required, and\n  existing configuration, conversations, attachments and workspace data remain",
